      "writtenOn": "2023-02-20T05:46:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s worth noting that contains is based on .equals, and .equals for records doesn\u0027t look at the TTL or receiptTimeMillis; so the address record TTL or receiptTimeMillis will never be updated, and I\u0027m guessing they\u0027ll just expire at some point (bug).\n\nNow I think TTL isn\u0027t used except for the service record, but the service record uses the same logic, so this probably causes services to expire after the initial TTL currently.\n\nMaybe file a bug to fix that ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 179,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 179,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "bbce9a5e743c218143b14947ed7d43a0c2b5a77c",
