      "writtenOn": "2023-02-20T05:46:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This changes the logic here: if the other result has records, it\u0027s always considered updated, even though it\u0027s possible that the new records are the previous ones (every call to addInet4AddressRecord returns false). With this code I think you\u0027ll send serviceUpdated callbacks for each incoming packet.\n\nTo avoid that I think you could do:\n\n - If there\u0027s any known record that is not in the \"other\" list, clear the records, with a TODO to only do it if the cache flush bit is set (b/266777103). This matches historical implementation that replaces all old records if new ones are received.\n - Then use `updated |\u003d addInet4AddressRecord(inetAddressRecord)`. This way if there\u0027s no change, updated stays false.",
      "revId": "bbce9a5e743c218143b14947ed7d43a0c2b5a77c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
